# Multi-tenant identity + onboarding

Phase 7 of the multi-tenant rollout. Hard rule 44 in
[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) is the source of truth.

## Hard rules

1. **Organization provisioning from Microsoft Entra ID claims goes
   through [`EntraTenantLink`](mdc:aqp/persistence/models_terraform.py)**
   (rule 44). Don't auto-create `Organization` rows from raw `tid`
   claims; the
   [`data.tenancy.link_org_to_entra_tenant`](mdc:aqp/data/mcp/tools/tenancy.py)
   admin tool (REST: `POST /tenancy/entra-links`) is the only
   sanctioned ingress.
2. **First-login provisioning lives in
   [`aqp/auth/user.py::_apply_entra_tenant_link`](mdc:aqp/auth/user.py).**
   Unknown `tid` + `auth_msal_b2b_enabled=True` creates a `pending`
   link; an AQP super-admin promotes via the
   [`EntraTenantLinkWizard`](mdc:aqp_client/src/components/onboarding/EntraTenantLinkWizard.tsx).
3. **The MSAL provider is registered by
   [`IdentityProviderMeta`](mdc:aqp/auth/providers/protocol.py).**
   Set `provider_kind = "msal_entra"` and the metaclass auto-
   registers. **Microsoft Entra ID is the platform's PRIMARY IdP**
   after the control-plane maturation (Phase 0.2); Auth0 stays
   registered as the B2C fallback for the self-signup pool +
   legacy deployments. The platform-core helper
   [`default_identity_provider_alias`](mdc:aqp_platform_core/src/aqp_platform_core/auth/__init__.py)
   returns `msal_entra` when `AQP_AUTH_PROVIDER` is unset; flip to
   `auth0` only for an explicit Auth0-first deployment. Both
   `aqp_admin` and `aqp_control_plane` consume the platform-core
   :class:`MsalEntraValidator` shim for inbound bearer validation
   without importing `aqp.*`.
4. **The multi-tenant authority is
   `https://login.microsoftonline.com/organizations`** by default
   (accepts users from any Entra tenant). Pin to
   `/{tenant_id}` for single-tenant; use `/common` to additionally
   accept personal Microsoft accounts.
5. **Frontend wiring:** SPA env vars are `VITE_MSAL_TENANT_ID` /
   `VITE_MSAL_CLIENT_ID` / `VITE_MSAL_AUTHORITY` /
   `VITE_MSAL_REDIRECT_URI` / `VITE_MSAL_SCOPES`. The
   [`AuthProvider`](mdc:aqp_client/src/lib/auth/AuthProvider.tsx)
   picks `@azure/msal-react` when MSAL is configured, else falls
   back to `@auth0/auth0-react`. The
   [`useAuth`](mdc:aqp_client/src/lib/auth/useAuth.ts) contract is
   unchanged so consumers don't branch.
6. **The Entra `oid` claim is the canonical user identifier**, not
   `sub`. `provision_user_from_claims` writes `oid` into
   `User.auth_subject` for `provider == "msal_entra"`.

## Don't

- Don't read `settings.<service>_client_*` for MSAL secrets. Resolve
  through [`CredentialResolver`](mdc:aqp/credentials/resolver.py)
  (Azure Key Vault store, AWS Secrets Manager, GCP Secret Manager,
  HashiCorp Vault — see Phase C in the plan).
- Don't bypass the M2M-secured
  [`/_internal/msal/sync`](mdc:aqp/api/routes/msal_sync.py) endpoint
  when an Entra Logic App / SCIM webhook needs to push user
  lifecycle. The endpoint mirrors `/_internal/auth0/sync` (same
  `require_m2m_token` dep).
- Don't auto-promote a `pending` EntraTenantLink without a human
  approver. The wizard / `link_org_to_entra_tenant` MCP tool is the
  only sanctioned ingress.
- Don't store secret values in the rendered onboarding wizard
  payloads. Email + tenant id + role mapping are not secrets;
  client secrets live in CredentialResolver.

